<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Guaxenduba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1614</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Guaxenduba was fought on 19 November 1614 on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. A Portuguese force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeronimo-de-albuquerque">Jerónimo de Albuquerque</a> defeated the French colonists of Equinoctial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupinamba">Tupinambá</a> allies, although it was outnumbered. The defeat led the French commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniel-de-la-touche">Daniel de La Touche</a> to surrender <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-luis">São Luís</a> in 1615, ending the French colony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-guaxenduba.jpg" alt="Battle of Guaxenduba" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: L. Gauthier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%89l%C3%A9vation_d%27une_croix_pour_la_b%C3%A9n%C3%A9diction_de_l%27Ile_de_Maragnan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
